<p>
  The HTTP <code>404 Not Found</code> response status code indicates that the server
  cannot find the requested resource. Links that lead to a
  <code>404</code> page are often called broken or dead links and can be subject to
  link rot.
</p>

<p>
  A <code>404</code> status code only indicates that the resource is missing: not
  whether the absence is temporary or permanent. If a resource is permanently removed,
  use the <code>410 Gone</code> status instead.
</p>
